  message: "From WI-hojib/WI-tagir (branch jgstern-agent/fix/hojib on top of WI-silos 41fd9834a6, not merged). PARTIAL overlap with this item's half (1), and a measured increase in half (2).\n\nHalf (1), the generic parameter used as a declared type, is now refused on the MEMBER path only. `_swift_member_type` refuses a property's type when it names a generic parameter of the declaring type, in Pass 1's field registry and in the binding pass. `_swift_type_parameter_names` now also collects a protocol's `associatedtype` names (hummingbird `associatedtype Responder` + `var responder: Responder { get }`).\n\nOn the 4-repo frozen A/B (origin/dev 385ec63be1 vs silos+hojib), generic-parameter or Self slots go 183 -> 170. Slots that left: Base x30 (KingfisherWrapper), Provider, Handler, S, M0/M1, ParentWriter, Parent, BaseChannel, BaseApp, Generator, CoreSequence, Delegate, Interceptor (a generic parameter shadowing the real Interceptor class).\n\nNOT done here, still this item's:\n- PARAMETERS typed by a generic parameter (`func f<C>(x: C)`): vapor C 8, T 12 remain.\n- `Self` as an emit-site type head: hummingbird has 131 `Self` slots on both arms.\n- A generic parameter of an EXTERNAL generic type that an extension adds members to: Alamofire `extension Result { var success: Success? }` -> `result.success.map` stamps `Success`, 2 sites, newly reached because member chains are now typed.\n- A typealias to a collection: Alamofire `typealias Object = [(key:..., value:...)]` -> slot `Object`, 3 sites.\n\nHalf (2), dotted nested project types in the slot, gets MORE exposure: 217 -> 234 rows on the same corpus, because member chains now reach more dotted-typed members (Kingfisher DiskStorage.Backend 63 -> 73, MemoryStorage.Backend 59 -> 64). The types are right; the slot policy is this item's defect. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/hojib.md and hojib/."  # 863c
